idual using existing in-memory recorder durations. git diff --check passed. Per operator instruction, local lint, typecheck, tests, builds, and gates were skipped; CI will be authoritative. Push is held until the current shared Gerrit CI runs drain.","timestamp":1787722007261501001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed Gerrit change 2234 from commit d5ea345ee0dc (Change-Id I50f5575d18227412aabf8202bc78e1c29e589fac). Gerrit and CI are now the validation authority; no local test, lint, typecheck, or build run was performed.","timestamp":1787722431319546001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed Gerrit change 2234 patchset 2 (8fb5eb7a) at operator direction before patchset-1 CI completed. This patchset contains only the classified lint-failure repair: Ruff I001 import ordering in completion_metrics.py and gate_dispatch.py; Change-Id I50f5575d18227412aabf8202bc78e1c29e589fac is preserved. Tracking the new CI run and both Gerrit labels; no force or rerun operation used.","timestamp":1787723300648963001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CI_RESULT {\"run_id\":\"32934525578\",\"status\":\"cancelled\",\"duration\":882,\"failure_type\":\"lint-failure\",\"failure_details\":\"Ruff I001 import ordering failed in completion_metrics.py and gate_dispatch.py; remaining test cells were cancelled when patchset 2 superseded the run.\",\"fixes_applied\":[\"Applied the exact import-order repair from Ruff\"],\"retry_count\":0}\nCI_RESULT {\"run_id\":\"32935422379\",\"status\":\"failed\",\"duration\":1344,\"failure_type\":\"lint-failure\",\"failure_details\":\"Ruff check passed; ruff format --check required a one-line condition in scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py. All test cells and all other gates passed.\",\"fixes_applied\":[\"Applied the exact Ruff one-line formatting change\"],\"retry_count\":1}\nPushed the resulting clean commit da9092d8 as Gerrit change 2234 patchset 3. Change-Id I50f5575d18227412aabf8202bc78e1c29e589fac remains intact. Local tests and gates were intentionally skipped per operator direction; CI is authoritative.","timestamp":1787724672571351001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CI_RESULT {\"run_id\":\"32937042550\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"duration\":1375,\"fixes_applied\":[\"Ruff import ordering repair\",\"Ruff one-line formatting repair\"],\"retry_count\":2}\nGerrit change 2234 patchset 3 completed all 19 CI jobs successfully. Local tests and gates remained intentionally skipped per operator direction.","timestamp":1787726054450055001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit change 2234 patchset 3 is fully ready except for LLM review: Verified +1 from CI run 32937042550, zero unresolved comments, and no LLM-Review vote. The review-bot briefly recovered and drained its queue from 23 to 10 while processing reviews, then its public /review/health endpoint returned sustained 502 responses before this change received a vote. No force/rerun operation was used. Submission and completion close remain pending ordinary review-service recovery.","timestamp":1787726823865801001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Gerrit change 2234 patchset 3 reached LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 with zero unresolved comments, then merged as 8559a0215b90e4ce361850e3a68583c35936ff22. CI_RESULT {\"run_id\":\"32937042550\",\"status\":\"passed\",\"duration\":1375,\"fixes_applied\":[\"Ruff import ordering repair\",\"Ruff one-line formatting repair\"],\"retry_count\":2}. Proceeding with ordinary completion verification from current origin/main; no force operation used.","timestamp":1787761010606831001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final workflow-field record from merged change 2234: verifier_precheck_context_ms contains child/bug closure checks plus ticket-context and declared-file-prefetch assembly; verifier_completion_agent_ms contains the verify agent, model calls, repository tools, bounded recovery, and finalizer; verifier_verdict_reconcile_ms contains deterministic normalization, citation resolution, and verdict-invariant enforcement; verifier_no_llm_passthrough_ms contains the deterministic short-circuit path; verifier_unclassified_workflow_steps_ms exposes any future timed leaf IDs without a mapping; verifier_workflow_residual_ms contains validation, expression/contract resolution, branch routing, recorder bookkeeping, terminal-result assembly, and integer-ms rounding outside leaf dispatch. These non-overlapping partitions reconcile to retained verifier_workflow_ms. The reducer adds no I/O or clock reads: it makes one bounded pass over existing in-memory recorder rows and constructs sidecar fields. Probe compatibility keeps older sidecars parseable. CI run 32937042550 passed all 19 jobs, including the focused emission/arithmetic and legacy-record coverage.","timestamp":1787761075553712001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787626705715675001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"37302e6e-f62d-4e8c-a5ca-fc9d01e5cfd7","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"0538-9893-97b2-4c2d"},{"link_uuid":"94640158-5ee4-4be1-bfa3-d0345f6f287c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1a02-b9a4-2d40-40ac"}],"description":"## Context\nThe completion-verifier sidecar now attributes wrapper time without a residual, but the largest inner interval is still exposed only as `workflow_ms`. That label hides the operations responsible for hundreds of seconds and cannot support performance diagnosis or expectation-setting.\n\n## Plan\n- Trace the completion workflow call path and define concrete, non-overlapping subphase boundaries whose sum explains `workflow_ms`.\n- Add monotonic duration measurements at existing seams only; instrumentation must not add LLM calls, Git work, filesystem snapshots, network requests, retries, or other material work.\n- Emit the named subphase durations in the completion sidecar while preserving existing aggregate fields and compatibility with older sidecars.\n- Extend the reusable duration probe to display and validate the new workflow breakdown and surface any remaining workflow residual explicitly.\n- Add focused automated coverage for metric emission, partition arithmetic, and legacy sidecars; rely on CI for execution because local resources are limited.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `workflow_ms` is broken into concrete operation-named, non-overlapping subphase durations.\n- [x] The subphase durations plus an explicit residual reconcile to `workflow_ms` within documented rounding tolerance.\n- [x] Instrumentation performs only in-process monotonic clock reads and sidecar field construction; it adds no LLM, Git, filesystem snapshot, network, retry, or subprocess work.\n- [x] Existing aggregate fields remain available and older sidecars remain parseable by the reusable probe.\n- [x] CI coverage verifies emission and arithmetic for the new fields and compatibility for old records.\n- [x] The final ticket record explains what each formerly generic workflow interval contains.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_metrics.py","reason":"Extract the completion metrics cluster and aggregate concrete workflow step durations without adding external work."},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py","reason":"Feed the existing recorder and workflow elapsed interval into the concrete phase aggregator while keeping the public aggregate."},{"path":"scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py","reason":"Name, report, and reconcile the new concrete completion workflow phases."},{"path":"scripts/rebar_duration_probe_support.py","reason":"Read the new sidecar fields while preserving older event compatibility."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_completion_wrapper_duration_instrumentation.py","reason":"Specify metric emission and partition arithmetic at the completion dispatcher seam."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_rebar_duration_probe.py","reason":"Specify probe reporting, source labels, residual handling, and legacy sidecar compatibility."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","1a02-b9a4-2d40-40ac"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"37784eab-7cdd-4662-8f2a-e50adcd245dd","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["observability","performance","completion-verifier"],"ticket_id":"3569-58fe-4303-4b78","ticket_type":"task","title":"Break down completion verifier workflow timing into concrete subphases","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["652debea-d5cf-4840-b770-db8b2f2ef60d","6a113fff-a219-40bd-8ad4-7166006e5dd6","61278833-eec5-4ad0-8146-6fb5a86361a8","f3cb481d-6f89-40f2-88d4-257f73e448a9","dcae5191-d046-44ab-a1a9-551ec75a6196","0c4a9b9f-c599-4579-b59a-a07ea470455e","94640158-5ee4-4be1-bfa3-d0345f6f287c","67665250-0b4b-4b91-8e42-8e0f20d599b8","829edfcd-a045-46e9-8400-059bcb451159","832778e7-bd5c-4943-af0a-ce833261606c","37784eab-7cdd-4662-8f2a-e50adcd245dd","48f9da7c-3c7a-4abe-b206-f9a8658b9adb"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787767918485598001,"uuid":"4d96a2f9-c760-4f2a-ba0a-308ea0ded710"}